# moon_supply

Keep a Moon AE2 watchlist at target counts by exporting from Earth AE2 into the Interplanetary Railgun Sender, then firing under Earth-controller command. Moon unloads itself. Items only (no fluids).

## Non-goals

- Fluids; full AE2-Moon dump; Moon receiver control
- In-flight accounting (flight 60 s, send pause 80 s; the next poll sees Moon AE already updated)
- Legacy fire-by-full as the primary mode for this sender (use `moon_supply` earth; standalone `railgun` is manual/legacy)

## Layout

### Earth (`entries/moon_supply_E_ctrl.lua`)

- Computer on wired net + ender modem **bottom**
- `meBridge_2` on AE2-Earth; exports straight into HV loaders via `exportItemToPeripheral` (optional `buffer` chest only if leftovers exist)
- Loaders: `tfg:hv_railgun_item_loader_in_20` … `_29` (`loader_prefix`, `expected | 10`)
- `redstone_relay` **top**, pulse **`back`**
- `monitor_1` — Moon stock / phase UI

### Moon (`entries/moon_supply_M_probe.lua`)

- Computer, ender modem **top**, ME Bridge on the **right** side (`bridge | right`)
- Stock probe only: answers Earth’s `stock_req` with `getItem` counts (no local watchlist)
- Railgun receiver unloads into Moon AE without this computer

## Behaviour

1. Poll Moon stocks: Earth sends watchlist ids in `stock_req`; Moon replies `stock_res` (protocol `tfg_moon_supply`). One source of truth — Earth’s cfg. Moon warms a full `getItem` cache once, then refreshes a rotating slice (~6 ids/req) so replies stay short on large ME.
2. Per item: `red_line = floor(target * red_frac)` (default `0.25`).
   - **ALARM** (global) if **any** item has `moon < red_line`
   - **WARN** if no ALARM but any `moon < target`
   - **OK** → idle
3. Build a shot package from deficits. Within a zone, cfg order. In **ALARM**, alarm items load before warn items of the same shot. **WARN** sends warn deficits only. Mid-shot, `mergePackage` expands wants from fresh Moon assess (e.g. gold dips while diamond crafts) — never shrinks in-flight wants.
4. Missing on Earth: try `craftItem` on the **final** item (AE expands multi-step trees itself). Prefer full ask →256→64→32→16→8→4→1; verify CPU job. Ghost success at a size falls back to a smaller ask (partial craft: 100 missing ingredients → 16 ok). **One ladder per id per pass**: a landed partial becomes a live job; the remainder is ordered once that job is gone (next ladder for that id this shot starts at 4× the last landed size). A pass stops after ~4 s of AE work and resumes at that id. Keep topping up after wait-collapse. Hard fails (`NOT_CRAFTABLE` / …, or an unclassified refusal when getItem says not craftable) → `craftStatus=no` + skip. «Нет в AE» comes only from a craft probe, never from `isCraftable=false` alone. Soft exhaust → `wait` («AE мало», not «Нет в AE») + 8 s cooldown, retry — never skip. Live AE jobs / pending survive into the next shot (status not wiped). `effectiveCraft` clamps craft vs earth+staged; opaque job shows `Крафт (1)` only while short. Row blinks `Крафт` ↔ `Загружено`; sys line shows live `крафт AE N в работе`.
5. After the first craft probe, only **hard** unobtainable ids (`craftStatus=no` / AE not craftable, no live job/stock) are dropped — even if some cargo is already staged. Soft `wait` stays in the package. If nothing remains, idle + `не шлём (нет в AE): …`.
6. During craft-wait (**ALARM 60 s** / **WARN 120 s**, or **3 s** if no AE jobs): export AE → loaders first each pass, then re-request craft as needed. Export: only `earth>0`; skip full loaders; ask the whole remainder per call (auto-falls back to 64/call if AP caps); two refusals for an id → stop it; max 12 `exportItem` calls/pass; 8 s cooldown after zero-move. **Collapse wait as soon as AE CPUs are idle**. Title stays short; debug ring shows timings.
7. **Fire** when the obtainable shot package sits in the loaders, or when every loader is cargo-full — but **not** while Earth still has obtainable stock/craft to push (`moreToLoad`). WARN zone rules unchanged; this only blocks early fire (e.g. diamond done, gold just merged). `загрузка` title only when loaders actually hold cargo. If the package cannot be finished after the wait, return to poll with a status note.
8. Pulse relay → `cooldown | 80`. Flight is 60 s, so the next poll sees the delivery. No in-flight reserve. A failed relay pulse does not start the cooldown.
9. **Parallel runtime**: `uiLoop` + `aeWatchLoop` + `moonWatchLoop` + `controlLoop`. Moon watch owns ender stock probes; control reads the cache (no competing rednet). AE watch refreshes Земля/Крафт (focus=active package; full every 8th, or every 16th when watchlist ≥30; slower when idle). Control exports/crafts/fires without owning long AE/Moon scans. `requestCrafts` schedules short package items (skips ids with live jobs), accounts for in-flight crafting (clamped), retries every 2 s. Snapshot: crafting-tasks first, then `getItem` fanned out over `ae_parallel` coroutines (cfg, default 8; `1` = sequential) so main-thread calls share ticks. Loaders: one shared scan (one `list()` per loader, parallel, size cached) reused by all loops for 0.5 s and invalidated by any cargo-moving export.

